    <l n="1" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="2">Praxiscum theoriâ conjungenda.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">§. 7.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Loca subjacentia sequuntur observan-</l>
    <l n="5">tiam, id est stylum urbis metropoli- tanae.</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="1" caput="12" para="true">LIBR. 4. INSTIT. TIT. 12.</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De perpetuis &amp; temporalibus actionibus.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">1. Proponuntur quaedam actionum divisiones.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">2. Tem-</l>
    <l n="11">pora actionum enarrantur.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">3. Quid moribus indicatur.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">1. Divisio actionum in nativas &amp; datIvas</l>
    <l n="15">rejicitur.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">2. Actiones rei persecutoria plerumque in</l>
    <l n="17">haeredes transeunt.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">3. Actiones poenales regulariter non tran-</l>
    <l n="19">seunt.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">4. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Si reus actori velit satisfacere non est</l>
    <l n="23">condemnandus.</l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="1" caput="13" para="true">LIBR. 4. INSTIT. TIT. 13.</l>
    <l n="25" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De exceptionibus.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">1. Non omne quod justum, statim</l>
    <l n="28">est aequum.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">2. Male quidam dividunt exceptiones in juris &amp; facti.</l>
    <l n="30" para="true">§. 1. 7.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">1, Exceptiones sunt juris gentium, habent</l>
    <l n="32">tamen formam a jure civili.</l>
    <l n="33">2. Exceptio quod metus, explicatur.</l>
    <l n="34">3. Quid sit exceptio doli?</l>
    <l n="35">4. Quid exceptio, si non per errorem?</l>
    <l n="36">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="37">1. Remissive agitur de exceptione</l>
    <l n="38">non numerata pecunia.</l>
    <l n="39">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="40">1. Exceptio pacti explicatur.</l>
    <l n="41">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="42">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="43">Quid sit exceptio jurisjurandi?</l>
    <l n="44">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="45">1. Exceptio rei judicatae cur detur?</l>
    <l n="46">2. Quae sint ejus requisita?</l>
    <l n="47">§. 8, 9, 10.</l>
    <l n="48">1. Exceptio alia est peremptoria, alia dila-</l>
    <l n="49">toria.</l>
    <l n="50">2. Quae appellentur exceptiones litis finis?</l>
    <l n="51">3. Natura dilatoriarum explicatur.</l>
    <l n="52">4. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="53">§. 11.</l>
    <l n="54">1. Declinatoria personae explicantur.</l>
    <l n="55">2. Procurator non debet esse infamis.</l>
    <l n="56">3. Quod moribus &amp; jure Canonico certum</l>
    <l n="57">est.</l>
    <l n="58" type="heading" level="1" caput="14" para="true">LIBRI 4. INSTIT. TIT.</l>
    <l n="59" type="heading" level="1" caput="14">14. De replicationibus.</l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">REplicatio ex aequitate introducta,</l>
    <l n="62">non ipso jure tollit</l>
    <l n="63">exceptionem.</l>
    <l n="64" type="foot" para="true">§. 1. Dilluitur objectio in l. 2. §. 3. D. de exceptionibus.</l>
    <l n="65">2. Mores explicantur.</l>
    <l n="66">3. De exceptione.</l>
    <l n="67">1. Exceptio vel in rem, vel in personam.</l>
    <l n="68">2. Etiam datur media seu mixta.</l>
